      "side": 1,
      "message": "This gives me some pause. Looking at (Section 7.3.10) in PD3.0 spec it says this deadline is governed by (tPSSourceOff 750-920ms Section 6.6.5.2) from ACCEPT-GoodCRC(*) which is a timer in the /SNK port partner/. (The only timer we, the SRC, should be watching is tSrcTransition holdup delay.)\n\nA timer timing out is not a valid exit condition for (PE_PRS_SRC_SNK_Transition_to_off), and does not exist in the spec. Thus I strongly suggest we do not add one here. We should follow spec.\n\nSee (Figure 8-116: Dual-Role Port in Source to Sink Power Role Swap State Diagram).\n\nHypothetically, if there is some sort of problem with silicon -- and it \"can\u0027t tell\" VBUS has been turned off -- I might suggest a board-specific driver \"hook\" workaround should be added elsewhere.",
